# Vue Router runs in "history" mode (createWebHistory), so real URLs like
# /umeghigido or /admin/lineages need to load the app's index.html and let
# Vue Router take over client-side — Cloudflare Pages otherwise has no
# server route for anything but the exact files it built, and would 404 on
# a direct visit or a page refresh on any route other than "/".
# Vite copies everything in /public into the root of /dist on build, so
# this file lands at dist/_redirects, which Cloudflare Pages reads
# automatically — no dashboard configuration needed.
/*    /index.html   200
